WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.560
The A-Z of isms... geocentrism.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.960
Until the 16th Century,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.400
geocentrism was a prevailing theory
of what the universe looked like.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.520
Geocentrism is the belief
that the Earth,

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.720
our home planet,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.360
is at the centre of the universe.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.920
Everything else revolves around us.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.320
This seemed obvious
to ancient astronomers,

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.360
after all they observed the sun and
the moon, the planets and the stars,

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.840
to move across the sky
as we go forward through time,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.480
just like we do today.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.000
So this must mean that the Earth
is in the centre of it all, right?

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.920
Wrong!

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.920
The earliest geocentric models
of ancient Greek

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.880
philosophers/scientists/general
all-rounders

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.800
such as Plato and Aristotle
in the 4th Century BC

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.160
placed a stationary
Earth at the centre

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.080
with the planets and the stars moving
around us on circles or spheres.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.960
The thing is,
the simple geocentric model

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.120
couldn’t quite explain all that
we see when we watch the skies.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.200
For a start,
the planets change brightness,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.200
which shouldn’t happen

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.240
if they're always
the same distance from the Earth.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.200
Second, the paths of Mars
and Jupiter through the sky

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.240
sometimes appear
to go backwards for a time,

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.440
which shouldn’t happen

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.720
if they're travelling round
in these neat little circles.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.400
Despite this,
the theory had such a hold

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.680
and astronomers were so
convinced by it

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.000
that they spent hundreds of years
making all sorts of modifications

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.080
to try and make
the general theory fit.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:26.720
And as needlessly complicated as it
now seems to modern astronomers,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.320
this version of the universe proposed
by Ptolemy in the 2nd Century,

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.560
was almost universally accepted
for hundreds of years.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.000
But not everyone was happy.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.120
As far back as the 3rd Century BC,

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.560
Aristarchus of Samos

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.560
had suggested that the Sun
was in the centre of the universe.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.040
And in the years that followed
Ptolemy's work

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.000
both European and Islamic scientists

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.680
started to question aspects
of his geocentric model.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.680
Finally in the 16th Century,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.000
Polish astronomer Copernicus
published his model of the universe,

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.880
which also put the Sun, not the
Earth, at the centre of it all.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.480
This is known as heliocentrism,

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.960
and for the first time,
mainstream science took note.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.840
Today we know that even heliocentrism
doesn’t tell the full story.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.320
While the Sun may be at the centre
of our solar system,

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.000
it is just one
of over a hundred billion stars

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.520
in our Milky Way galaxy,

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.560
which is itself one of over
a hundred billion galaxies

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.960
in the observable universe.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.360
Not only do we have to contend

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.280
with being just one of probably
countless planets out there,

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.440
modern cosmology tells us
that the Earth and our solar system

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.280
doesn't even occupy
a special place in the universe.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.080
And in fact, it turns out that there
is no centre to this universe at all.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.080
Thanks for watching.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.280
